{# Accessibility & Scaling #}
<section>
    <h2>Accessibility & Responsive Scaling</h2>

    <p>One of the key advantages of Q units is that they respect user preferences and scale across different devices:
    </p>

    <div class="code-block">
        <pre><code>// Q units automatically scale with the html font-size
// User sets 18px font size: q(16) becomes 1.125rem (18px)
// User sets 14px font size: q(16) becomes 0.875rem (14px)

// Your CSS stays the same
.component {
  padding: q(16); // Always 1rem, but scales with user preference
}</code></pre>
    </div>

    <div class="alert alert--tip">
        <p class="alert__title">Browser Zoom & User Preferences</p>
        <p>REM-based units respect browser zoom levels and user font-size preferences, making your designs accessible to
            users who need larger text.</p>
    </div>
</section>
